  "lighting": {
    "recipe": [
      "Render the map and sprites as usual (albedo).",
      "Light = ambient (per room kind, below) + the sum of every light: colour x power x flicker[frame] x falloff.",
      "Falloff = max(ground pool, source sphere): the pool is a 2:1 ellipse on the floor under the source, the sphere is round around the source itself, both (1 - d)^1.6 out to the light's radius in tiles.",
      "Band the light into steps of 1/7 with a 4x4 ordered dither, so pools step like pixel art.",
      "Lit = albedo x min(light, 1.3). Emissive pixels (prop slots glow / flame / liquid, texture slot glow) skip this: they keep their own colour, then the usual bloom picks them up.",
      "Optionally lay light/vignette.png over the view for the room's edges."
    ],
    "godot": "Equivalent with real lights: a CanvasModulate / WorldEnvironment ambient of the room colour, an OmniLight3D (or PointLight2D) per manifest light at its 'at' point, colour and radius, energy driven by the flicker curve, and an unshaded material (or emission) on the emissive slots.",
    "ambient": {
      "crypt": [
        0.25,
        0.27,
        0.4
      ],
      "cave": [
        0.26,
        0.33,
        0.46
      ],
      "hall": [
        0.3,
        0.25,
        0.26
      ]
    },
    "flicker": {
      "torch": [
        1.0,
        0.9,
        1.06,
        0.94,
        0.84,
        1.02,
        0.92,
        1.08
      ],
      "fire": [
